{"term":"uncover","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:61e9cdc4c490e80a4d","definition":"To remove a cover from.","example":"The model railway was uncovered.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["uncloak","uncoif","unhat"],"antonyms":["cover up"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["uncoverable","uncoverer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/uncover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f8c7ad6bba1af08c7e","definition":"To reveal the identity of.","example":"The murderer has finally been uncovered.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["uncloak","uncoif","unhat"],"antonyms":["cover up"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["uncoverable","uncoverer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/uncover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:356df1f4e305447699","definition":"To show openly; to disclose; to reveal.","example":"To uncover his perjury to the oath of his coronation.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["expose"],"antonyms":["cover up"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["uncoverable","uncoverer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/uncover#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:de27570fd278aa953e","definition":"To remove one's hat or cap as a mark of respect.","example":"Alfred, surprised to meet his father, whom he thought absent from home, […] stood, holding his firelock in one hand, and his hat in the other, having uncovered himself as soon as he perceived his father.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["doff"],"antonyms":["cover up"],"collocations":[],"usage":"reflexive","register":"intransitive, reflexive","wordFamily":["uncoverable","uncoverer"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary